      "id": 1,
      "text": "Leopoldstadt was named after Leopold I, Holy Roman Emperor, after Jews were expelled and the area was renamed “Leopold’s city.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leopoldstadt",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Augarten park houses the Vienna Boys’ Choir and a porcelain factory that displays regular exhibits in its foyer.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leopoldstadt",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Once called “Mazzesinsel” for its deep Jewish roots, Leopoldstadt now blends old‑school kosher bakeries with third‑wave espresso spots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitcity.travel/en/vienna/district/leopoldstadt",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Prater amusement park’s historic Ferris wheel, the Wiener Riesenrad, sits beside the lush Grüner Prater park and draws visitors worldwide.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitcity.travel/en/vienna/district/leopoldstadt",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Leopoldstadt’s Museum für Unterhaltungskunst chronicles clowns, circuses, and even blind education, offering a quirky slice of cultural history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leopoldstadt",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The district’s summer cinema tradition continues with open‑air screenings at Augarten and other venues, echoing Vienna’s long‑standing film culture.",
